From 28f76ff49f5a893268a2ccecf5e098a207f2e6df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:55:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 141/144] fix: keep Crytek's cloud reach; only the seam fades
 (edge fade stays, sky-ray unclamp removed)

User (2026-09-09): "I want to change on the basis of Default. Forcing the clouds to extend
is not wrong as an idea, but that is not how it works when you go outside." Low clouds
dissolve into the atmosphere; they do not run crisply to the horizon. So the reach is
Crytek's again - the depth-buffer clamp at the far plane and the max viewable distance are
back exactly as stock - and only the seam is treated: the sky-ray edge fade from d6f4c52f
remains, unconditional, so the cloud region's sky blends into the plain sky below over the
last 4 km of marched segment through every camera. Clouds.cfx vs stock is now that one block
in each visible technique. Overlay: "cloud edge fade yes (ReCS, all cameras)".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
---
 .../GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp          |  2 +-
 .../GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricClouds.cpp     | 18 +++----
 .../GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricClouds.h       |  2 +-
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Clouds.cfx     | 50 ++++++++-----------
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp
index 2038bfc6..5ace847f 100644
--- a/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp
+++ b/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/ToneMapping.cpp
@@ -1184,7 +1184,7 @@ void CToneMappingStage::DisplaySceneReferredCoverage()
 		{
 			const float sunLum = 0.2126f * cl.sunExposed.x + 0.7152f * cl.sunExposed.y + 0.0722f * cl.sunExposed.z;
 			const float skyLum = 0.2126f * cl.skyExposed.x + 0.7152f * cl.skyExposed.y + 0.0722f * cl.skyExposed.z;
-			cry_sprintf(str, "  clouds [on] x%.4g: sun %.4g  sky %.4g  atmos-sun %.4g  zenith haze %.4g exposed (%+.1f stops vs grey)  sky rays past ZF + edge fade %s (ReCS, all cameras)  | Rayleigh k %.3g/m unexposed by design",
+			cry_sprintf(str, "  clouds [on] x%.4g: sun %.4g  sky %.4g  atmos-sun %.4g  zenith haze %.4g exposed (%+.1f stops vs grey)  cloud edge fade %s (ReCS, all cameras)  | Rayleigh k %.3g/m unexposed by design",
 			            cl.exposureApplied, sunLum, skyLum, cl.atmosSunExposed,
 			            cl.zenithHazeExposed,
 			            (cl.zenithHazeExposed > 0.0f) ? log2f(cl.zenithHazeExposed / 0.18f) : -99.0f,
diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricClouds.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/RenderDll/XRenderD3D9/GraphicsPipeline/VolumetricClouds.cpp
